{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01Mg7MEnUqn6eamQXYBEB7tx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q6: LLM confidently wrong — debug RAG giving confident wrong answers?**\n\n**The core framework:**\n\n1. **RAGAS as the diagnostic crosshair** — `context_recall` vs `faithfulness` isolates whether the failure is in the retrieval layer or the generation layer. These require completely different fixes.\n\n2. **Retrieval failure path** (`context_recall` low): check chunking boundaries → vocabulary mismatch (add BM25 hybrid + RRF) → top-k too low (add cross-encoder reranker) → stale index (CDC incremental ingestion).\n\n3. **Generation failure path** (`faithfulness` low): set `temperature=0` → add explicit grounding prompt → fix lost-in-the-middle reordering → reduce top-k / raise cosine threshold to cut context pollution.\n\n4. **Production safety net**: async DeBERTa NLI entailment gate — if entailment < 0.80, serve canned abstention instead of the confident wrong answer. Billing-bot example: 4.2% → 0.6% confident-wrong rate.\n\n**Key pitfall called out:** Candidates who jump straight to \"fine-tune the model\" or \"lower temperature\" without first running RAGAS to identify which layer is broken."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":359,"cache_read_input_tokens":66930,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":359,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70a59e59-6b37-4ab0-b5b5-a3634e3f78a7","uuid":"be916356-92b1-4ba2-9365-d70892871ce1"}
